  "result": "`compareVersions` is added and committed as `f90d688`, and `npm run fast` passes (biome, boundaries, tsc and the related tests).\n\n- **Function:** `compareVersions` in `src/cli/semver.ts` returns -1, 0 or 1. It compares parts numerically, so `1.2.10` is greater than `1.2.9`. Missing trailing parts count as zero, so `1.2` equals `1.2.0`. Anything that isn't dotted digits (`''`, `1.`, `v1.2`, `1.2-beta`) throws a `TypeError`.\n- **Test:** `test/cli/semver.test.ts` uses node:test and covers ordering, equality, padding, very large parts and invalid input.\n- **Notes:** the plan and progress are in `docs/notes/compare-versions.md`.\n- **Shard weight:** I also added a weight entry for the new test in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`. The repo's rule test `test/rules/shard-weight-coverage.test.mjs` fails without one. I set it to 0.1, a local estimate, since CI hasn't measured it yet.\n\nThe commit isn't pushed and there's no PR. I didn't run the full `npm run gate`.",
